ed in canada 5000  others have been approved but are still  waiting overseas for those trapped  inside taliban controlled afghanistan  evacuation efforts have stalled and as  jeff semple reports the delayed efforts  just cost one girl her life  speaking by phone from afghanistan  bashir tells me his ten-year-old  daughter nazifa was very bright at the  top of her class  she was learning english and really  excited to move to canada he says we're  protecting bashir's identity because he  worked for the canadian forces in  kandahar after the taliban took over in  august his family was approved to move  to canada but they're stuck with no way  out of the country  last week beshear's family was driving  past a taliban checkpoint they thought  the guard was waving them through but  then one of the talibans started  shooting at their vehicle the bullets  struck and injured his brother-in-law  and his niece bashir's daughter nasifa  was shot in the head and didn't survive  it's unclear why they were targeted but  bashir believes it was because he had  worked for the canadians  i am lost my daughter is gone and i'm  afraid for the rest of my family he says  there's a ten-year-old girl who was shot  in the face  when she should have been on her way to  canada i can say that with no doubt in  my mind this was on this was avoidable  uh and it was bound to happen  five months since ottawa announced its  special afghan refugee program thousands  who supported canada's military are  still in hiding many still waiting for  ottawa to process their applications we  cannot stay here anymore this former  interpreter submitted his application  last summer and hasn't received a  response but he did receive this letter  from the taliban ordering all those who  have worked with foreigners to appear in  court or the islamic emirate will deal  with them according to its laws he's  considering turning himself in to save  family daughter and my wife are crying  the  his  you know crying  for 